We’re looking for a professional to strengthen our team!

At the Bancorbrás Group, every idea is welcome, and we value proactive, creative, and self-motivated individuals who are driven by a customer-first approach, excellence, transparency, and diversity.

If you enjoy working in a collaborative, diverse, and innovative environment, come join our team and make a difference!

Be part of a solid, people-oriented company that turns life goals into reality!

- Architecture and Prototyping: Design and implement efficient backend architectures using .NET 8+ / C# 12 in rapid, experimental deployments;

- API Development and Performance: Develop agile and secure APIs using Minimal APIs, Entity Framework Core, Dapper, and Redis;

- Agility Patterns: Apply pragmatic approaches to DDD, CQRS, and messaging tailored to the needs of each experiment;

- Messaging and Integration: Structure event-driven integrations using RabbitMQ, MassTransit, and SQL/NoSQL;

- Resilience and Cloud: Configure fault tolerance (Polly), basic observability, and deployments in containers and Azure;

- Applied Innovation: Explore new AI tools and patterns to continuously improve the Innovation team’s deliverables.

- Education: Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology or a related field;

- .NET Ecosystem: Solid prior experience as a .NET/C# Architect with expertise in Core, EF Core, and relational and non-relational databases;

- Messaging and Events: Hands-on experience implementing event-driven architectures;

- Pragmatic Approach: Demonstrated ability to make independent technical decisions focused on balancing quality and agility;

- AI for Development: Understanding of AI applications in the development lifecycle (Prompt Engineering, LLMs, Agents, and MCP).

Desired Qualifications:

- Practical experience with AI frameworks such as Semantic Kernel and Azure OpenAI;

- Knowledge of Event Sourcing;

- Active technical portfolio (GitHub, personal projects, or prior experience in the startup ecosystem).

Additional Information

Bancorbrás Benefits

🌴Attendance Bonus: Three days off per year to enjoy as you wish;

📚Education Assistance: A real incentive for your growth! 50% coverage of courses focused on your professional development, available after 1 year with the company;

🏡Work-from-Home Allowance: An extra monthly amount to help with the costs of remote work;

🧸Daycare Assistance: Additional support for those with children under 6 years of age;

🧑🏼‍🎄Christmas Gift Basket: At the end of the year, receive a special bonus to celebrate with your family;

🩺Health Insurance: Nationwide coverage with copayments;

🦷Dental Plan: Smile worry-free! A comprehensive plan to take care of your oral health;

🏦Private Pension Plan: The company contributes alongside you to ensure greater financial security;

🔒Life Insurance: Peace of mind for today and tomorrow. Protection so you can live with greater ease and security;

✈️TRIB PASS – Leisure and Tourism Platform: Discover incredible experiences more easily. Bancorbrás subsidizes 50% of the monthly fee, and you enjoy the rest;

💳Food/Meal Vouchers (Caju Card): Granted for each day worked and widely accepted. You choose how to use them: for everyday shopping or meals;

🏋🏽Wellhub (Gympass): Exercise, health, and wellness! Access to thousands of gyms through the most comprehensive fitness platform.
<p>Apply directly on <a href="https://remotejobs.org">RemoteJobs.org</a>: https://remotejobs.org/remote-jobs/net-software-architect-innovation-ai-grupo-bancorbrs</p>

We currently have a vacancy for a Power BI Developer in English, to offer his/her services as an expert who will be remotely within EU. In the context of the first assignment, the successful candidate will be integrated in the Development team of the company that will closely cooperate with a major client’s IT team on site.

Tasks:

- Analyze functional and technical designs prepared by the project team;

- Propose a data storytelling and UX design approach with consistent visuals to improve the user experience;

- Review existing reports, propose and implement enhancements; 

- Prepare mockups and/or prototypes of the requested dashboards and report, present these to business owners and end-users to gather their feedback; 

- Organize dashboards and reports so that the most important data (notably KPIs) are immediately visible (the "at-a-glance" principle) and navigation between them is intuitive; 

- Design a SharePoint site to provide a consolidated view of the dataset catalogue, dashboards and reports and other DWH resources;

- Support automation initiatives based on DWH datasets, reports and dashboards, to increase efficiency;

- Collaborate and support other DTS staff and consultants (Power Platform, Azure, SharePoint) on the integration of DWH Power BI reports with other solutions.

Requirements

- Relevant University degree (i.e. Information Systems, Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, etc.) with significant coursework in Graphic Design, Communication, or Marketing Analytics;

- Minimum of five years of experience in UI/UX design and the implementation of high-quality dashboards;

- Data Storytelling & UX Design: The ability to translate complex data into a coherent narrative. Understand how to organize dashboards so that the most important KPIs are immediately;

- DAX Proficiency (Calculated Measures): Even if the datasets are ready, advanced DAX will be needed to create dynamic, user friendly measures (like year-over-year growth, moving averages, or conditional formatting logic) that drive the visuals; 

- Ability to apply Power BI visual best practices, including selecting appropriate visuals and avoiding unnecessary or distracting elements;

- Customization & Formatting: Expert knowledge of the "Format" pane, themes, color palettes for accessibility (color-blind friendliness), and interaction settings (drill-throughs, bookmarks, and slicer synchronization); 

- Dashboard Navigation: Building intuitive interfaces using buttons, navigation bars, and landing pages (i.e. SharePoint pages) to make the reports and dashboards feel like an application rather than separate items;

- Certification required: Power BI Data Analyst Associate (PL-300) or equivalent;

- Other professional certifications in design/data storytelling, UI/UX design or human-computer interaction (HCI), Power BI, Azure SQL are valuable;

- Excellent command of the English language.

Benefits

If you are seeking a career in an exciting and dynamic company, where you will offer your services as part of a team of a major European Institution, operating in an international, multilingual and multicultural environment where you can expect real chances to make a difference, please send us your detailed CV in English, quoting reference: (20262/09/2026).

We offer a competitive remuneration (either on contract basis or remuneration with full benefits package), based on qualifications and experience. All applications will be treated as confidential. 

You may also consider all our other open vacancies by visiting the career section of our web site (www.eurodyn.com) and follow us on Twitter (@EURODYN_Careers) and LinkedIn. 

EUROPEAN DYNAMICS () is a leading Software, Information and Communication Technologies company, operating internationally (Athens, Brussels, Luxembourg, Copenhagen, Stockholm, London, Nicosia, Hong-Kong, Valetta, etc). The company employs over 1000 engineers, IT experts and consultants (around 3% PhD, 36% MSc and 53% BSc or equivalent). We design and develop software applications using state-of-the-art technology. The group generates annual revenues in the range of EURO 40 million, with an EBITDA in the range of 20%. The value of our contract portfolio exceeds EURO 300 million. EUROPEAN DYNAMICS is a renowned supplier of IT services to government institutions, multinational corporations, public administrations and multinational companies, research and academic institutes.

As part of our dedication to the diversity of our workforce, we are committed to Equal Employment Opportunity without regard for race, color, national origin, ethnicity, gender, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, or religion

EUROPEAN DYNAMICS (ED) adheres to the General Data Protection Regulation principles by applying its Privacy Policy as published in www.eurodyn.com/privacy. By submitting an application to this position and by sharing your personal data with ED, you acknowledge and accept its Policy and authorize ED to process your personal data for the purposes of the company's recruitment opportunities, in line to the Policy.
